\caption(All16 joint probabilities from the untrained toy network, in integer-state order. They sum to one without any across-image softmax. Normalization follows the causal factorization, not a reconstruction-score normalization.)
\alttext(A line shows the probabilities of all16 four-bit configurations; their native summed probability is one.)

> Derive the probability mixture rather than average the losses

After fitting two independent normalized joints p_R and p_V, the source mixes
their **probabilities**, p_mix(x)=(p_R(x)+p_V(x))/2. If l_R and l_V are per-image
joint NLLs, the stable calculation is

$$ l_{mix}=-\left[m+\log(e^{-l_R-m}+e^{-l_V-m})-\log2\right],\quad
m=\max(-l_R,-l_V). $$
\alttext(The equal-probability mixture NLL is negative logsumexp of negative joint NLLs plus log2, using a stabilizing maximum.)

It is not(l_R+l_V)/2. Jensen gives l_mix<=mean(l_R,l_V) for each image;
it does not guarantee a lower test-pool mean than the better individual model.
Its component derivative is the posterior responsibility
p_k(x)/(p_R(x)+p_V(x)). The stabilizing maximum can be stopped while keeping the
correct first and higher derivatives of logsumexp.

For two normalized four-state tables A=(.4,.1,.1,.4), B=(.1,.4,.4,.1), the
mixture is uniform(.25,.25,.25,.25), NLL=log4. Averaging the two component NLLs
instead gives log5 at each state. The native helper accepts joint NLL sums,
not per-pixel means; otherwise it would mix a different quantity.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md_mixture_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto t=n::DType::Float64;
 auto p=n::tensor({.4,.1,.1,.4,.1,.4,.4,.1},{4,2},t);
 auto nll=(-n::log(p)).requires_grad_();auto out=n::models::EqualDensityMixture(nll);
 auto average=n::mean(nll,{1});
 auto derivative=n::grad(n::sum(out.per_image_nll),{nll})[0];
 if(n::max(n::abs(derivative-out.responsibilities)).item()>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Responsibilities");
 if(std::abs(n::sum(n::exp(-out.per_image_nll)).item()-1)>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Mixture normalization");
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 plot.points({0,1,2,3},average.to_vector<double>(),"Mean NLL",{220,38,38},6)
 .points({0,1,2,3},out.per_image_nll.to_vector<double>(),"Probability mixture",{37,99,235},6)
 .y_limits(1.25,1.95).x_label("Four-state outcome").y_label("Joint NLL in nats")
 .title("A probability mixture differs from mean component NLL").save_svg("build/md_mixture_toy.svg");
 std::print("Mixture mean={:.8f}; mean component NLL={:.8f}; first responsibility pair={}.\n",out.mean_nll.item(),n::mean(average).item(),n::take_rows(out.responsibilities,{0}).values_str());
}
```
