> Trace the actual64-pixel network and its fixed degree inventory

Raster degrees are1..64; reverse degrees64..1. Hidden1[i]=1+floor(i*62/15)
and hidden2[i]=hidden1[(5*i)mod16],i=0..15. Both orderings have the same raw
initial weight draws with seed8803, but different structural masks and independent
optimizer states. Three affine layers64→16→16→64 have2304 kernel values and96
bias values:2400 stored in6 leaves,1144 forbidden and1256 active.

The source trains one store for each fixed order. It does not train a shared-weight
order-agnostic model. Changing a native per-call order flag is possible, but
would be a different experiment if used to share learned weights across orders.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8803);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){
  auto out=n::models::MadeDensity(p,x,false);
  n::model_stage("Degree-masked64 to16 sigmoid",x,out.hidden1);
  n::model_stage("Degree-masked16 to16 sigmoid",out.hidden1,out.hidden2);
  return n::model_stage("Strict-mask16 to64 logits",out.hidden2,out.logits);
 },"Raster MADE:2400 stored /1256 active values");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
 options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=4;
 auto fig=model.plot(n::zeros({1,8,8,1}),options);
 if(fig.parameter_count()!=2400||p.size()!=6)throw std::runtime_error("Source census");
 fig.save_svg("build/md_network.svg");
}
```
