> Keep the baseline and both fixed learning histories visible

The fit-only independent Bernoulli baseline estimates each site's posterior
q_j=(count_j+.5)/1001. Test NLL uses its unrounded Double posterior; archived
probability images are separately Float32. This preserves the original scalar
protocol. Neither validation nor test data fits those baseline probabilities.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
