> Check current and future exclusion in the correct order

Each model differentiates every raw output logit with respect to all64 raw
inputs. All current/future entries in its **own degree order** are exactly zero.
At each of64 ordinals it also flips all current/future raw bits simultaneously,
requiring every prefix conditional to remain bit identical. These128 finite-change
guards complement8192 Jacobian entries. A single image matches its output inside
the full200-row test batch. In the archive, Jacobian rows and columns remain raw
raster indices even for reverse order; conditionals instead remain ordinal-indexed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md_causality.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
 for(const std::string order:{"raster","reverse"}){
  n::Tensor j;for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/made_density/"+order+"/causality.npz"))if(key=="jacobian")j=n::abs(value);
  auto scaled=n::log1p(100*j);scaled=scaled/n::max(scaled);panels.push_back(n::reshape(scaled,{64,64,1}));
 }
 n::save_image_grid(n::stack(panels),"build/md_causality.png",2,0,1,3,.5,4);
}
```
