> Interpret complete-image mixture responsibilities

For a held-out complete image, softmax(−joint NLL) describes which fixed-order
component contributes more probability to the equal mixture. These are posterior
component responsibilities, not learned mixture weights, digit-class probabilities
or an accuracy score. The source does not generate new mixture samples. A
proper mixture sampler would first choose one order for a whole image and then
sample that component, not average the two incompatible per-pixel conditionals.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md_responsibilities.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::Tensor weight;
 for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/made_density/mixture_summary.npz"))if(key=="responsibilities")weight=value;
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();auto x=n::arange(0,200).to_vector<double>();
 plot.points(x,n::slice_axis(weight,1,0,1).to_vector<double>(),"Raster component",{37,99,235},2)
 .points(x,n::slice_axis(weight,1,1,2).to_vector<double>(),"Reverse component",{220,38,38},2)
 .y_limits(-.02,1.3).x_label("Held-out pool row in original source order").y_label("Posterior component responsibility")
 .title("A complete image can favor either fixed-order joint").save_svg("build/md_responsibilities.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/md_responsibilities.svg)
// result_end

\caption(All200 held-out complete images contribute one responsibility pair summing to one. The index is source row order, not time. Prior component weights are fixed at one half; the plotted posterior weights vary with each image's two joint likelihoods.)
\alttext(Blue raster and red reverse responsibility points complement each other around one half across200 test images.)

> Preserve numerical fidelity without overstating the result

An independent development NumPy oracle checks139110 forward values,470400
analytic partials,36 scalar finite differences, all192 Adam writes and6000
fitting-row visits. It verifies4800 degree/mask values,8192 causal derivatives,
128 order-correct future flips and10752 sampled pixels. Every forbidden weight
and partial stays exact. The report must reproduce47 original archives/2799518
values,576 phase captures and the equal-probability joint-mixture array before
retirement. Preparation and execution use the native API, without a TensorFlow
runtime or another checkout.

The two source orders and their normalized probability mixture are retained in
full. The best individual test score remains reverse order at.55103, and every
reported density still loses to the fit-only baseline. The experiment verifies
causal degree constraints, order-aware sampling and a valid joint-density mixture;
it does not claim shared-weight order-agnostic training, classifier accuracy,
state-of-the-art likelihood or realistic image generation.

